<blockquote>
<p>Most chemical testing of biological materials is destructive. How did they analyze genetics or THC content when the stuff is indestructible excluding when it's in a blunt wrap?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Once it's been burned by the user, presumably the smoke and ashes could be collected and analyzed. It wouldn't be the ideal method, but remember that the whole point of smoking is to vaporize the chemicals inside of the plant matter while leaving them semi-intact, and they're not lacking in samples.</p>

